UID:114900-1793986200-1794002400@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Museum Movie Night: Jurassic Park
DESCRIPTION:Jurassic Park (1993)\n“Yeah\, but\, John\, if The Pirates of the Caribbean breaks down\, the pirates don’t eat the tourists.” \nHold onto your butts; science just brought dinosaurs back to life! Step into a theme park where cloning meets chaos\, and T. rex steals the show. It’s a thrilling mix of cutting-edge science\, prehistoric power\, and popcorn-worthy adventure that reminds us: just because we can\, doesn’t mean we should. \nThis movie is rated PG-13. \nMuseum Movie Night — a night of movies\, music\, and mind-blowing fun. Before the show\, enjoy live tunes\, hands-on science activities\, and tasty food and drinks. After the credits roll\, stick around for a science chat with an expert and movie trivia\, all hosted by A/V Geeks! \n  \nCheck out the upcoming movies and learn more about Museum Movie Night: Where Science meets the Cinema. \nBuy Tickets \n\nSchedule\n5:30pm–7pm: Live music and science stations. Food and drinks for sale.\n7pm: Movie begins in the WRAL 3D Theater\, followed by commentary and movie trivia. \nStay after the movie for trivia and Q&A with our expert\, Dr. Jennifer Anné\, Assistant Manager of the SECU DinoLab \n \n\nExhibits and Activities\nSimply saying that proteins\, uh… preserve \nMeet the paleoproteomics team from NCSU\, the real miracle workers when it comes to ancient molecule preservation. Learn what is possible\, and what is not\, in the world of dino molecules. In addition to the modern molecular world\, learn how the science fiction of Jurassic Park inspired scientist to start digging into the realm of ancient molecular studies with our local science historian\, Dr. Elizabeth Jones. \nDino Dig \nSee what mini treasures you can excavate! \nPaper Circuits \nLearn how circuits work and create a light-up card to take home! \nDino DNA Craft \nChoose a dino\, shrink it\, and pop it in a test tube! You never know when you’ll need some dino DNA! \nThey Could Be Dinos \nWell…maybe not\, but these live animals have some prehistoric vibes!
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/museum-movie-night-jurassic-park/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,General Events,Museum Movie Night,Special Events,Teens,WRAL 3D Theater
ORGANIZER;CN="Miranda%20Dowdy":MAILTO:miranda.dowdy@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Downtown Raleigh 11 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=11 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6395502,35.7822735
END:VEVENT
