UID:124348-1794306600-1794317400@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Roots of Discovery: Festival of Lights
DESCRIPTION:Experience the vibrant traditions of India and explore the connections between cultural heritage\, science and the natural world. Celebrate the Festival of Lights through the traditions and stories that have been passed down through generations. Learn how Indian contributions to astronomy\, mathematics\, medicine and more shaped how people understand the world around us. Join us to discover the ideas that still spark curiosity\, creativity and innovation today. \n\nPresentation\n1pm–1:30pm\, SECU Daily Planet Theater\nThreads of Genius: India’s Legacy in Global Science\nFrom the invention of zero to quantum physics\, understanding the genetic code and space exploration\, India has continually expanded humanity’s scientific horizon from antiquity to the present. Learn about landmark discoveries and the Indian origin scientists who reshaped global knowledge. \nAbout the Speaker\n\nDr. Manisit Das holds a PhD in Pharmaceutical Sciences from the UNC Eshelman School of Pharmacy and works in medical strategy\, connecting scientific research with clinical practice and patient outcomes in respiratory diseases. Originally from West Bengal\, India\, he earned his BSc and MSc in Chemistry at the Indian Institute of Technology Kharagpur. He has called North Carolina his home for the past decade. \nActivities\nLights from Within \nNC Museum of Natural Sciences\nExplore how different animals from the depths of the oceans to the leaves of the forest create light in a process called bioluminescence. Find out how animals use light\, often invisible to the human eye\, to communicate and find food. \nPoses and Perspectives: The Origin and Evolution of Yoga \nTarang Mental Health\nYoga originated in Northern India over 5\,000 years ago. Learn about the original science and practice of yoga and how it evolved into the modern forms practiced today. \nKalaatattva: The Elements of Art \nChani Jain\nIndian dance is more than movement — it is a living philosophy where rhythm\, expression\, and devotion come together to tell timeless stories. Learn about the beauty of Indian dance forms\, the philosophy and culture that shape every movement. You’ll go home knowing how to recognize beats and build your own patterns\, so that you can dance with ease and confidence. \nCricket: The Tie that Binds a Billion People\nCore Cricket and the Morrisville Raptors\nAttitude\, energy\, enthusiasm and imagination are all you need — besides a bat and a ball. Learn about the sport that has captivated a billion people for over 400 years. \nPainted Traditions: The Story of Henna\nHenna Art by Nadia\nFor thousands of years\, henna has adorned hands across North Africa\, the Middle East and South Asia to celebrate weddings\, holidays and life’s milestones. Discover the roots of this ancient art and see how centuries of tradition come alive in every design.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/roots-of-discovery-festival-of-lights/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adults,All Ages,Children,General Events,SECU Daily Planet Theater,Teens
ORGANIZER;CN="Hugo%20Romero-Sanchez":MAILTO:hugo.romero@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
